---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/05-07/';
const plan='https://www.psirep.com/system/files/792-00069-1-summit11000fpg.pdf_-_792-00069-summit11000fpg.pdf';
const vendor='https://www.coltronics.com.au/DATA/Summit_SS.pdf';
const refs=[
 ['front','Front and microscope bridge','Facility guide p. 3 establishes the platform, centerline, platen and vertical reference. Exact objective revision not identified.',plan+'#page=3'],
 ['loading','Rollout chuck access','Summit family cover photo and AP configuration, pp. 1, 15. A shield and drawer are modeled; hinge and loading stroke are inferred, not metrology specs.',vendor+'#page=15'],
 ['tips','Platen, two DC manipulator arms and chuck','Summit data sheet pp. 2–4. Capable of multiple manipulators; reconstruction populates two DC positions and a synthetic resistor coupon.',vendor+'#page=3'],
 ['rear','Rear panel and external instrument','Side/top drawing establishes occupied envelope, not connector part numbers. Cable paths and external SMU shell here are illustrative.',plan+'#page=3']];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Summit 11000B-AP · probe station" description="Place two microscope-aligned probes on a passive resistor coupon, test an I–V sweep, then lift one probe and identify an open circuit." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment ps">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/05-07/">← Equipment 05-07</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#ps-ref">References</a><a href="#ps-check">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">05-07 · WAFER ELECTRICAL METROLOGY</span><h2>Summit 11000B-AP</h2><p>Cascade Microtech / FormFactor manual MicroChamber station with a room-temperature 200 mm chuck, two DC probes and a separate ideal source-measure unit. This bench positions probes and routes terminals; it does not itself supply current.</p></header>
<div class="ps-grid">
<section><span class="eq-meta">01 / INSPECT</span><h3>Microscope and platen</h3><div id="ps-stage" aria-label="Orbitable metric Summit probe station"></div><div class="bar">{['Overall','Load bay','Positioners','Rear','Bench'].map(x=><button data-ps-view={x}>{x}</button>)}<button id="ps-xr" hidden>Enter VR</button></div><p id="ps-ready" role="status">Loading model…</p><p class="small">Drag to orbit, pinch to zoom. Select the shield, tray, positioner tips and bench instrument in the model. The source is separate from the station.</p></section>
<section><span class="eq-meta">02 / POSITION</span><h3>Align and land the tips</h3><div class="bar"><button id="ps-shield">Open shield</button><button id="ps-drawer">Extend drawer</button><button id="ps-load">Load standard</button><button id="ps-link">SMU connected</button></div>
<div class="options"><label>Stage X (mm)<input id="ps-x" type="number" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>Stage Y (mm)<input id="ps-y" type="number" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>Chuck θ (°)<input id="ps-theta" type="number" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>Probe to position<select id="ps-tip"><option value="0">HI</option><option value="1">LO</option></select></label><label>Tip X (µm)<input id="ps-tipx" type="number" step="any"/></label><label>Tip Y (µm)<input id="ps-tipy" type="number" step="any"/></label><label>Tip gap (µm)<input id="ps-gap" type="number" step="any"/></label><label>Contact per tip (Ω)<input id="ps-ohm" type="number" step="any" value="0"/></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="ps-stage-apply">Apply stage pose</button><button id="ps-tip-apply">Apply probe pose</button><button id="ps-land-hi">Land HI</button><button id="ps-land-lo">Land LO</button></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="ps-demo" class="primary">Run 1 kΩ resistor example</button><button id="ps-run">Measure I–V</button><button id="ps-blk">Load Keithley example settings</button></div>
<p id="ps-status" aria-live="polite">Fixture loaded; both probes retracted.</p>
<details><summary>Import coupon or source settings</summary><p>Open the shield and extend the drawer before loading a <code>bts.probe-coupon.v1</code> netlist. Imported <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-03/">09-03 SourceMeter</a> files reuse requested voltages, dwell and current limit only; actual current is recalculated from these contacts. Match the sample ID and polarity.</p><input id="ps-import" type="file" aria-label="Coupon or SourceMeter JSON" accept=".json,application/json"/><p><a href={p+'coupon-example.json'}>Coupon</a> · <a href={p+'keithley-setup.json'}>SourceMeter example</a> · <a href={p+'contract.schema.json'}>Schema</a></p></details>
</section>
</div>
<section><span class="eq-meta">03 / OBSERVE</span><h3>Microscope alignment and electrical readout</h3><div class="ps-grid"><div><canvas id="ps-scope" width="760" height="420" aria-label="Metric top-down microscope alignment, showing probe centers and die pads"></canvas><p class="small">Select HI or LO, raise it, and click a pad in the alignment view to move that probe in X/Y. The reticle is a metric rendering, not an optical image.</p></div><div><canvas id="ps-iv" width="600" height="300" aria-label="Terminal voltage versus current plot"></canvas><output id="ps-results">No sweep.</output><div class="bar"><button id="ps-json" disabled>Export contact sweep (JSON)</button><button id="ps-csv" disabled>Export readings (CSV)</button><button id="ps-wave" disabled>Export settled volts for replay</button></div></div></div></section>
<section><h3>Passive experiment and compatibility</h3><p><strong>First run:</strong> both tips contact 100 µm pads on a nominal 1 kΩ teaching resistor. At +1 V the connected coupon draws +1 mA. Lift either probe and run again: the source still requests voltage, but the open route has zero current and no inferred resistance. Slide a raised tip outside its pad or rotate the chuck to see the effect of alignment.</p>
<p>A probe is electrically connected only when its center lies in exactly one pad rectangle after the inverse stage transform and its gap is ≤50 nm (ideal contact threshold). The engine solves Kirchhoff’s current law for passive resistors only, drops 1 V across the two touched nets and uses R = 1 V/I. Two optional constant contact resistances are added in series. The external ideal source applies V/R with a current clamp and records both requested and terminal voltage. Open circuits are explicitly null resistance; no fictitious leakage is added.</p>
<p><strong>Limits:</strong> ±2 V, 1 µA–5 mA compliance, 2–201 points, up to 32 electrical nodes. No semiconductor junction, contact force, tangency, heating, EMI, guarding, leakage, RF, noise or Z actuation of the fixed chuck. No real hardware is controlled. The <a href="/simulations/equipment/10-02/">10-02 Digidata</a> accepts the same analog waveform format for replay of settled DC voltage points; this does not represent measurement transients or an electrical attachment. This fixture’s 11-point example independently replayed at 10 Hz with no overload and 134.28 µV peak quantization residual.</p></section>
<section id="ps-ref"><span class="eq-meta">04 / GEOMETRY</span><h3>Reference sheet</h3><p>Original renders alongside linked primary references. The vendor planning drawing's microscope height is <strong>811 mm + 100 mm</strong>, not a single 1006 mm dimension; this model uses the 811 mm nominal setting. Record originally listed “FormFactor 11000B”; AP is one documented family configuration. Exact serial revision and rear connector positions remain unknown.</p>
<div class="figs">{refs.map(([id,title,detail,url])=><figure><img src={p+id+'.webp'} alt={'Original Summit model: '+title} loading="lazy"/><figcaption><b>{title}.</b> {detail} <a href={url}>Source</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value and conditions</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>External envelope</td><td>862 × 831 mm W×D, nominal height 811 mm with additional microscope travel. Closed station without bench instrument.</td><td><a href={plan+'#page=3'}>Facility guide 792-00069-1 p. 3</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Manual stage</td><td>203 × 203 mm, 5 mm per turn; fixed Z; θ ±5.7°, 0.8°/turn. Continuous ideal motion in simulator; no positioning accuracy claimed.</td><td><a href={vendor+'#page=2'}>Summit datasheet p. 2</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Platen / chuck</td><td>745 × 595 × 20 mm steel platen, 200 mm selected chuck. Center height, feeds and local probe arm dimensions inferred.</td><td><a href={vendor+'#page=3'}>Summit datasheet p. 3</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Manual shield and rollout</td><td>–1.55 rad and +235 mm modeled inspection strokes; visual drawer clearance drop is inferred; unverified actual travel. Probe lift 300 µm default in teaching fixture.</td><td><a href={vendor+'#page=15'}>AP platform options, p. 15</a></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="ps-check"><span class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION</span><h3>Reference checks</h3><p>Independent calculations, scaled geometry and browser interaction only, not validation of a physical instrument.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>1 kΩ coupon, +1 V</td><td>1.000 mA</td><td>1.000 mA</td><td>1 nA</td><td>Pass</td></tr>
<tr><td>Raise HI by 1 µm</td><td>0 A / open</td><td>0 A / open-contact</td><td>1 fA</td><td>Pass</td></tr>
<tr><td>Independent resistor network + contacts</td><td>1010 Ω</td><td>1010 Ω</td><td>0.001 Ω</td><td>Pass</td></tr>
<tr><td>Clamp at 0.5 mA, request +1 V</td><td>0.500 V</td><td>0.500 V</td><td>1 µV</td><td>Pass</td></tr>
<tr><td>Keithley upstream request, same coupon</td><td>11 source points</td><td>11; current matches</td><td>1 nA</td><td>Pass</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={p+'acceptance.json'}>Original cases</a> · <a href={p+'verification.json'}>Verification report</a> · <a href={p+'contact-example.json'}>Contact example</a> · <a href={p+'open-example.json'}>Open example</a> · <a href={p+'settled-volts.json'}>Replay example</a> · <a href={p+'summit-11000b.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable model</a> · <a href={p+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR anchors and render budget</a></p><p class="small">Optional WebXR configuration and named metric controls share the browser state. No physical Quest validation.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/05-07/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.ps{max-width:80rem}.ps-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.3fr) minmax(17rem,1fr);gap:1.25rem}.ps section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:.85rem 0;padding:.85rem 0;min-width:0}.ps h2{margin:.22em 0}.ps p{line-height:1.45}.ps label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;gap:.25em}.ps .options,.ps .figs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.bar{display:flex;gap:.45rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.65rem 0}.ps button,.ps select,.ps input{font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);min-height:2.35rem;border-radius:.16rem;padding:.4rem .5rem;min-width:0;max-width:100%}.ps button{cursor:pointer}.ps button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}.ps .primary{color:#fff;background:#204752}.ps #ps-stage{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,32vw,445px);background:#d1d9db;touch-action:none}.ps #ps-stage :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.ps #ps-scope,.ps #ps-iv{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.ps #ps-results{font-family:monospace;display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.5rem 0}.ps code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.small,.ps figcaption{font-size:.88rem}.ps figure{margin:0}.ps img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.ps table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.88rem}.ps th,.ps td{padding:.45em;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}.ps #ps-status.error{color:#ac492e}.ps [hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:790px){.ps-grid,.ps .figs{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
